# Build context exclusions for builds that use the repo root as context:
#   - root Dockerfile           (docker build -t ... --build-arg MODULE_NAME=<module> .)
#   - */Dockerfile via Jenkins  (buildAndPush uses context '.')
#
# Both compile from source inside the maven stage, so nothing here is needed at
# build time. Without this file the context is ~2.7GB, which makes every build
# spend 2+ minutes on "load build context" and intermittently kills BuildKit
# with "error reading from server: EOF".
#
# NOTE: builds that use a subdirectory as context (GitHub Actions passes
# ./billops, ./xamops-service, ./frontend-app, ./media-ops-service) do NOT read
# this file — they read <subdir>/.dockerignore. In particular the CI images for
# xamops-service and media-ops-service do `COPY target/*.jar`, and the **/target
# rule below cannot affect them.

# --- Version control & tooling metadata (341MB) ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agent
.agents
.kiro
.postman
.superset
.playwright-mcp
.tmp-stubs

# --- Node dependencies and frontend build output (1.2GB) ---
# The frontend image builds from ./frontend-app as its own context and runs
# `npm ci` itself, so neither is ever needed from the root context.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/vite.config.js.timestamp-*

# --- Maven output (531MB) ---
# Every root-context Dockerfile runs `mvn clean package`, which regenerates these.
**/target

# --- Python virtualenvs and caches (299MB, forecast-service/venv) ---
**/venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# --- Prebuilt Go agent binaries (101MB) ---
xamops-agent/xamops-agent_linux_*
xamops-agent/xamops-agent_darwin_*
xamops-agent/xamops-agent_windows_*

# --- Local runtime artifacts (99MB) ---
# **/logs, not logs: modules keep their own (e.g. xamops-service/logs).
**/logs
**/*.log
my-vault
preview_*.png

# NOTE: xamops-service/src/main/resources/static/agent/ holds the ~101MB of
# prebuilt agent binaries the service serves from its download endpoint. They
# are git-tracked and must stay in the jar, so they are deliberately NOT
# excluded here — they are most of the remaining build context.

# --- Docs, tests and local compose/config not used by the JVM build ---
docs
postman
jmeter-tests
eks
scripts
opensre
**/README.md
**/CONTRIBUTING.md
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Jenkinsfile
.dockerignore
